    "['tunnel-selector [parameter1] permit node [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set policy-options policy-statement s1 term 10 then next policy p1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set policy-options policy-statement s1 term 10 then next policy p1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `tunnel-selector` command:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement s1 term 10 then next policy p1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, tunnel selection is typically handled through routing policies (`policy-statement`) rather than a dedicated tunnel-selector construct\\n- The `then next policy p1` directive achieves similar behavior to Huawei's `apply tunnel-policy p1` by forwarding matching traffic to the specified tunnel policy\\n- The `term 10` corresponds to Huawei's `node 10` for policy sequencing\", 'trans_template': 'set policy-options policy-statement s1 term 10 then next policy p1'}]]": 1,
