    "['vsi [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe `vsi v1` command in Huawei creates a Virtual Switch Instance (VSI) for L2VPN/VPLS services. In Juniper, the equivalent is creating a routing instance of type VPLS. The Juniper command establishes the foundation for VPLS configuration, similar to how VSI does in Huawei's implementation.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls'}]]": 1,
    "['pwsignal bgp', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls'], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `pwsignal bgp` command:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet\\nset routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn control-plane bgp\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the VPLS signaling is configured under the routing-instance (equivalent to Huawei's VSI) with BGP specified as the control protocol. The `encapsulation-type ethernet` is typically required for L2VPN services. The exact syntax might vary slightly depending on the Junos version.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn control-plane bgp', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls'], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `pwsignal bgp` command:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet\\nset routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn control-plane bgp\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the VPLS signaling is configured under the routing-instance (equivalent to Huawei's VSI) with BGP specified as the control protocol. The `encapsulation-type ethernet` is typically required for L2VPN services. The exact syntax might vary slightly depending on the Junos version.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn control-plane bgp'}]]": 1,
    "['route-distinguisher [parameter1]:[parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1;', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet'], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nroute-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1;\\n##\\n\\nFor Juniper devices, the equivalent command would use the same syntax but with a semicolon at the end (Juniper's JUNOS convention). The RD format (ASN:nn or IP:nn) remains identical between Huawei and Juniper implementations.\", 'trans_template': 'route-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1;'}]]": 1,
    "['vpn-target [parameter1]:[parameter2] import-extcommunity', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-target import target:100:1', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet'], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-target import target:100:1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, the equivalent of Huawei's VSI (Virtual Switch Instance) is typically configured under `routing-instances` with type `vpls` or `l2vpn`.\\n- The `vpn-target` in Huawei translates to `vrf-target` in Juniper.\\n- The import-extcommunity is specified using the `import` keyword.\\n- The target community format changes from `100:1` to `target:100:1` in Juniper syntax.\\n- I assumed the VSI `v1` would be configured as a routing instance named `v1` in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-target import target:100:1'}]]": 1,
    "['vpn-target [parameter1]:[parameter2] export-extcommunity', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet'], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent combines both the import and export VPN targets into a single `vrf-target` statement, which serves the same purpose as Huawei's separate `vpn-target` commands. The `route-distinguisher` is also shown as it's typically configured together with the target communities in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'set routing-instances v1 protocols l2vpn encapsulation-type ethernet'], 'root': 'set routing-instances v1 instance-type vpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent combines both the import and export VPN targets into a single `vrf-target` statement, which serves the same purpose as Huawei's separate `vpn-target` commands. The `route-distinguisher` is also shown as it's typically configured together with the target communities in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1'}]]": 1,
