    "['policy vpn-target', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1', 'parent_command': ['set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'family l2vpn signaling'], 'root': 'set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper command translation for `policy vpn-target`:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-import import-policy\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-export export-policy\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, VPN target policies are typically configured under routing instances (similar to VSI in Huawei). The translation assumes:\\n1. `v1` is the routing-instance name (equivalent to VSI v1)\\n2. The import/export policies would need to be separately defined to match the Huawei behavior\\n3. Juniper uses `vrf-target` for the BGP extended community (similar to vpn-target in Huawei)\\n\\nThe actual implementation might require additional policy configuration depending on the specific requirements.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-import import-policy', 'parent_command': ['set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'family l2vpn signaling'], 'root': 'set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper command translation for `policy vpn-target`:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-import import-policy\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-export export-policy\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, VPN target policies are typically configured under routing instances (similar to VSI in Huawei). The translation assumes:\\n1. `v1` is the routing-instance name (equivalent to VSI v1)\\n2. The import/export policies would need to be separately defined to match the Huawei behavior\\n3. Juniper uses `vrf-target` for the BGP extended community (similar to vpn-target in Huawei)\\n\\nThe actual implementation might require additional policy configuration depending on the specific requirements.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-import import-policy'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-export export-policy', 'parent_command': ['set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'family l2vpn signaling'], 'root': 'set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper command translation for `policy vpn-target`:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-import import-policy\\nset routing-instances v1 vrf-export export-policy\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, VPN target policies are typically configured under routing instances (similar to VSI in Huawei). The translation assumes:\\n1. `v1` is the routing-instance name (equivalent to VSI v1)\\n2. The import/export policies would need to be separately defined to match the Huawei behavior\\n3. Juniper uses `vrf-target` for the BGP extended community (similar to vpn-target in Huawei)\\n\\nThe actual implementation might require additional policy configuration depending on the specific requirements.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances v1 vrf-export export-policy'}]]": 1,
